# When two branches each add their own entry to CHANGELOG.md's
# [Unreleased] section, git's default merge produces a conflict even
# though the right resolution is "keep both." `merge=union` tells git
# to take both sides of conflicting hunks, in order, with no markers.
# This is the right behavior for append-only logs like a CHANGELOG.
#
# It is NOT the right behavior for source code; do not extend this rule
# casually. If you find yourself wanting it for another file, think
# hard about whether you really mean "additive log" or whether you
# should be reordering or de-duping entries by hand.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
